analysisWe need to read code and comment. The comment is:

```java
// @@@ If both initial capacity and capacity increment are non-negative, then the size of the vector is zero.
```

We need to produce an assert statement reflecting this.

We are in constructor:

public Vector(int initialCapacity, int capacityIncrement) {
    super();
    if (initialCapacity < 0)
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Illegal Capacity: "+
                                           initialCapacity);
    this.elementData = new Object[initialCapacity];
    this.capacityIncrement = capacityIncrement;
    // @@@ If both initial capacity and capacity increment are non-negative, then the size of the vector is zero.
}

So after constructor finishes, we need to assert that if both initialCapacity >=0 and capacityIncrement >=0 then size() == 0.

